      "sceneId": "scene_007",
      "type": "talking_point",
      "heading": "What You Can Actually Do",
      "narration": "Here's the practical takeaway. If you have elevated liver markers like AST and ALT, glycine supplementation is remarkably easy to try. The study used about 100 milligrams per kilogram of body weight. It has a slightly sweet taste \u2014 no choking down bitter pills. You could measure your liver markers, supplement for two weeks, and measure again. It's a simple, low-risk self-experiment backed by real, if early, science.",
